<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dongmyeong of Goguryeo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">58–19 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a> · Also known as King Dongmyeong, Go Jumong</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dongmyeong, known as Jumong, was the founder of Goguryeo, traditionally in 37 BCE. Korean legend makes him the son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuhwa">Yuhwa</a> and a heavenly father, raised at the court of Eastern Buyeo, from which he fled south to found his kingdom at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jolbon">Jolbon</a> in the Yalu valley. He is honoured on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gwanggaeto-stele">Gwanggaeto Stele</a> as the dynasty's founder, and the Baekje royal house also claimed descent from him.</p></div>
